{
  "_comment": "Effect recipes for WRFx (WRFx.h lists the names gameplay uses). Each effect is layers of sprites from the atlas (Tools/fx/make_fx_atlas.mjs: dot, spark, smoke, smoke2, flame, flame2, flare, ring, chip_wood, chip_stone, leaf, shard, flake, droplet, glow, wisp). blend 'add' glows (fire, sparks, magic), 'lit' is smoke and debris lit by the scene. count = burst, rate = per second while a looping effect runs (loop: true). life/size/speed/spin/rot are [min, max] (s, cm, cm/s, deg/s, deg). grow = end size x start. dir is in the effect's frame (X = its rotation's forward; impacts face along the surface normal or away from the blow), spread = cone half-angle. gravity x 980 cm/s2 (negative rises), drag 1/s, turbulence cm/s2, stretch = streak length x speed. radius (sphere, or disc/ring), box half-extents, line (along X) and lift place the spawn; radial flies out from the centre. scale (from the caller) multiplies sizes (scaleSize false: not) and spawn shapes, speeds only with scaleSpeed, counts by scale^countExp. follow = moves with the effect. sortBias (cm) layers flat lit sprites (bigger = drawn first, underneath). bounce = lands on the ground and bounces. colors = linear RGBA over the sprite's life. intensity = HDR glow (add) or self-glow (lit). light = a pooled point light (seconds = fade for one-shots, flicker for loops). shake = tuning.json fx.shake.<name>. Live-reload with the console command WR.FxReload.",

  "handSockets": ["LeftHand", "RightHand", "mixamorig_LeftHand", "mixamorig:LeftHand", "hand_l", "hand_r"],

